From: Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net>
Date: Thu, 10 Apr 2025 15:15:36 +0200
Subject: Fix GHSA-3cr5-j632-f35r: Null byte in hostnames

This fixes stream_socket_client() and fsockopen().

Specifically it adds a check to parse_ip_address_ex and it also makes
sure that the \0 is not ignored in fsockopen() hostname formatting.

(cherry picked from commit cac8f7f1cf4939f55f06b68120040f057682d89c)
(cherry picked from commit 36150278addd8686a9899559241296094bd57282)
(cherry picked from commit d407d8a8735ebf43bee3e6b49fb013b8aa4b6bfc)
(cherry picked from commit 4066d405ab8ac17b3d366f2bf9f1eaa9fc707012)
(cherry picked from commit 0f05651a8ccf817e9817073537ce622f5161c735)
(cherry picked from commit 8aad7c1186bfc4c81399564e3657cd285189dbe1)
(cherry picked from commit cd4b3e44ae797627f599927ba9a93c672a08b7ad)

debian-php-backports: ported to PHP 5.4.45 (php5 5.4.45-0+deb7u30): the
fsock.c change is unchanged. In xp_socket.c the same NUL byte check is added
at the start of parse_ip_address_ex(); 5.4 already declares p inside the IPv6
branch, so moving that declaration is not needed.
